      "session_total_notional_list_value_usd": 0.306,
      "notes": "A hole in the tag run. The rule splits it into two arcs, which is indistinguishable from a genuine re-invocation. Known and accepted -- the register treats re-invocation as a boundary anyway, so both readings agree on the boundary. Asserted here so the behaviour is pinned rather than merely documented: if Claude Code ever drops the tag mid-run, arcs fragment and per-routine cost shatters, and this test says so out loud."
